{
  "version": "1-ablated-test-matching",
  "purpose": "Non-diagnostic intent taxonomy for the relevance gate (Phase 8.3, reason (b)). A query is refused for intent only when non-diagnostic intent dominates: at least one intent term, NO diagnostic cue word, and NO DTC code.",
  "authoring": [
    "Built from GENERAL non-diagnostic intent categories, terms named in the Phase 8.3 brief, and the DEV out-of-scope queries. TEST out-of-scope queries were NOT consulted while building this list.",
    "provenance: general = standard non-fault intent vocabulary; user = named in the 8.3 brief; dev_oos = taken from a DEV out-of-scope query.",
    "Safety rule (automated, src/gate.py audit): no intent term may occur in any manual DTC description, cause, effect or checkpoint - a real fault query that echoes the manual must never trip the intent filter. Ambiguous words are therefore omitted on purpose: 'available/availability' (the manual has 'heater unavailability' as a fault), bare 'seat' (valve seat), bare 'ac' (AC voltage), 'supply' (supply voltage), 'order' (firing order).",
    "Diagnostic cues are words that signal a fault. Any cue in the query vetoes an intent refusal, so a fault query that happens to mention price, a dealer or a warranty still passes.",
    "Terms match on word boundaries, case-insensitive, tolerating a plural 's'. matches_test_query flags are COMPUTED only after this file is frozen (see docs/report/phase8_3_relevance_gate.md)."
  ],
